Below is a complete Jenkins **Shared Library** layout (Groovy) implementing all requested capabilities:

- **(1) Automated version bumping** from **Conventional Commits**
- **(2) Multi-branch pipeline support** with **env-specific configuration**
- **(3) Artifact signing** with **GPG keys**
- **(4) Credentials health check**: reads Jenkins credentials, verifies expiration, tests connectivity to external services, and posts a secured audit record to `https://jenkins-audit.internal/health`
- **(5) Kubernetes deployment with **Helm**
- **(6) Post-deployment canary analysis**

> Notes / assumptions:
> - This library is intended to run in a Jenkins controller with the credentials plugin installed.
> - “Read all Jenkins stored credentials” is not realistically possible in a portable way without using Jenkins internal APIs. The code below uses standard internal Jenkins APIs (`com.cloudbees.plugins.credentials.*`).
> - “Verify expired” relies on credential types exposing expiration metadata (mostly `StandardUsernamePasswordCredentialsImpl` via `getExpirationDate()` and similar types). Not all credential types carry an expiration date.
> - “Test connectivity to each external service” requires you to map credential IDs to connectivity checks. The library provides a pattern + mapping hook you can extend.
> - “Logs the credential values” to an audit endpoint is extremely sensitive. The code below supports **redaction** by default and requires explicit config to include values. In almost all real setups you should not log raw secrets.

